<title>USA: Motorola begins construction of U.K. plant.</title>
<headline>Motorola begins construction of U.K. plant.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON HEIGHTS, Ill. 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc's Cellular Infrastructure Group said Wednesday it began work on its new $116 million manufacturing headquarters in Swindon, Britain.</p>
<p>Motorola said it acquired the site last year. The first phase of development will be 315,000 square feet of manufacturing and office space, ready for occupation in 1998.</p>
<p>Motorola provides wireless communications, semiconductors and advanced electronic systems, components and services.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
